# The lines the Slang twin of this vertex stage may declare differently from the GLSL (task 0072, stage b), read by
# SlangPermutations in components-tests. "glsl-only: <line>" or "slang-only: <line>"; every listed line must occur, so
# a stale entry fails the test.
#
# The texture coordinates: the GLSL declares an array sized by the specialization constant numUvSets (constant_id 0,
# lib/attributes.glsl), which Slang cannot place; the twin declares the first set only, at the same location. The sky
# reads only the first set, and a pipeline may supply more attributes than a shader reads.
glsl-only: in location=3 array1(vec2f32)
glsl-only: spec_constant id=0 i32
glsl-only: spec_constant_default id=0 bits 1
slang-only: in location=3 vec2f32
# Unused vertex inputs: the GLSL declares attributes it never reads (lib/attributes.glsl declares every one its
# defines name); Slang drops unused entry parameters. The pipeline's vertex input state is built from the defines, not
# from the shader, so it is unchanged.
glsl-only: in location=1 vec3f32
